  "note": "Borough election polled Wednesday 17 May 1967 (results declared 18 May); twenty candidates for twelve councillorships over the whole borough. Unionists won every seat; Mrs. Monroe, a former mayor, topped the poll, and T. Ross (unaffiliated Unionist) was bottom with 748."
